     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x2022;	CSOs organized knowledge sessions about: environmental impact of onshore and offshore wind parks, biodiversity in raw materials, environmental due diligence, risks of child labour occurring in minerals, public procurement, risks and negative impact in mica mining. 
&#x2022;	CSOs gave input and shared knowledge and expertise in different working groups: working group Due Diligence, working group Collective Action &amp; Increasing Leverage, working group Tender and Procurement
&#x2022;	CSO gave advice to companies, for example on tenders in the wind sector (ecological impact and mitigation was given as input). Also, a guiding document on biodiversity impact was written for the wind sector. 
&#x2022;	Advice was given on grievance mechanisms
&#x2022;	CSOs gave input on tools that were developed by SER for members (supplier assessment questionnaire, code of conduct, heat map, guidance on engagement with suppliers on forced labour. 
